  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ai4scholar.net?src=dsh\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/literaf/dsh-ai4scholar/main/docs/logo.svg\" width=\"120\" alt=\"AI4Scholar\"></a></p>\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>dsh-ai4scholar</strong></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "English | [中文](README_CN.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-ai4scholar) [](https://github.com/literaf/dsh-ai4scholar/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [](https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin)\n\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://ai4scholar.net?src=dsh\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/literaf/dsh-ai4scholar/main/docs/ai4scholar-home.jpg\" alt=\"ai4scholar.net\" width=\"100%\"></a></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Academic literature tools for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (`dsh`), delivered as 38 native agent tools — the same coverage as the AI4Scholar plugins for OpenClaw, Codex, and Hermes. Powered by [ai4scholar.net](https://ai4scholar.net?src=dsh)."
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "| Family | Tools | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Paper search** | `search_papers` — Semantic Scholar only by default; select PubMed, arXiv, or Google Scholar via `sources` as needed. Multiple sources are merged by DOI / arXiv id / PMID / title, with multi-platform hits ranked first | per selected platform |\n| **Semantic Scholar** (200M+ papers, all fields) | `search_semantic`, `search_semantic_bulk`, `search_semantic_snippets` (full-text excerpts), `search_semantic_paper_match` (title → paper), `get_semantic_paper_detail`, `get_semantic_paper_batch`, `get_semantic_citations`, `get_semantic_references`, `get_semantic_paper_authors`, `search_semantic_authors`, `get_semantic_author_detail`, `get_semantic_author_batch`, `get_semantic_author_papers`, `get_semantic_recommendations`, `get_semantic_recommendations_for_paper`, `download_semantic`, `read_semantic_paper` | credits |\n| **PubMed** (biomedical & life sciences) | `search_pubmed`, `get_pubmed_paper_detail`, `get_pubmed_paper_batch`, `get_pubmed_citations`, `get_pubmed_related` | credits |\n| **Google Scholar** (broadest coverage, cited-by counts) | `search_google_scholar` | credits |\n| **arXiv** | `search_arxiv`, `download_arxiv`, `read"
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "**Start with one source.** Omitting `sources` (or passing `[]`) queries only Semantic Scholar. For biomedical or clinical topics, select `sources: [\"pubmed\"]` as appropriate. Use multiple sources, such as `[\"semantic-scholar\", \"pubmed\"]`, when broader coverage is explicitly requested or one source is insufficient. Each billed API request adds to the charge; Google Scholar bills per page, while arXiv is free. If Semantic Scholar is disabled, the default is the first enabled platform in this order: PubMed, arXiv, Google Scholar."
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Every paper-list tool returns one normalized record shape — title, authors, year, venue, citation count, DOI/PMID/arXiv ids, URL, open-access PDF, abstract — so the model (and Code Mode programs) can chain calls across platforms without special cases. Results render as citation cards in the dsh Web UI; full-text tools return the PDF text in slices (`offset` / `max_chars`) so a 40-page paper never floods the context."
    },
    {
      "section": "AI4Scholar for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "**Credits are visible.** Every billed tool card in the chat carries the charge in its title (`Semantic Scholar: protein folding · 10 credits · 4,990 left`), the model-facing result ends with `AI4Scholar credits — this call: 10 · this session: 40 · remaining: 4,960` (from the API's `X-Credits-*` headers) and the model is asked to close a billed turn with a one-line credit note; `/ai4scholar` renders a balance card (available credits, breakdown, membership, key status, session spend) and `get_ai4scholar_credits` gives the model the same numbers. Free platforms (arXiv, bioRxiv/medRxiv, DOI) carry no credit line."
    },
    {
      "section": "Screenshots",
      "text": "| API key card (legacy Settings view) | `/ai4scholar` balance card |\n|---|---|\n|  |  |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "**Quick start** (macOS / Linux; Windows PowerShell is the same):\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "0. Prerequisites: Node.js ≥ 22.19 (or ≥ 24) and pnpm (dsh manages plugins with pnpm)",
      "text": "node -v\nnpm i -g pnpm                     # skip if you already have it"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh\ndsh --version"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. This plugin (into the web profile; use --profile headless for the CLI runner)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ai4scholar"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "dsh web                           # prints http://127.0.0.1:3080\n```\n\nThen, once, in the browser:"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "1. **Settings → Models** — paste your DeepSeek API key ([platform.deepseek.com](https://platform.deepseek.com)).\n2. **Plugins → Installed → dsh-ai4scholar** (or **Settings → AI4Scholar**) — paste your AI4Scholar API key ([ai4scholar.net](https://ai4scholar.net?src=dsh)) and press **Save**. The card stores it in the dsh credentials store (`$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml`, mode 0600, the same place the Models page keeps provider keys), tests it at once (`✓ Key works · 89,419 credits available`), and it takes effect on the next tool call — no restart. A **Refresh** link re-checks any time; the browser never sees the key (the check goes through the plugin's host route `GET /ai4scholar/balance`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "On current DSH Desktop, click **dsh-ai4scholar** in the sidebar’s **Plugins → Installed** list: the key form is visible immediately on its detail page. **Settings → Built-in plugins** is a host inventory, so it no longer contains this form. Older Harness versions still offer the original **Settings → Plugins → AI4Scholar** card. Existing keys keep working; all entrances use the same credential reference."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "Pick a workspace folder and ask away. Upgrades: `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ai4scholar@latest`, then restart `dsh web`."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "Prefer files or CI? The plugin resolves the credential reference `AI4SCHOLAR_API_KEY`, so any of these also work (highest precedence first): `export AI4SCHOLAR_API_KEY=…` in the shell that launches dsh · a line in `$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml` · a line in the project or `$DSH_HOME/.env`. The card reports which layer is supplying the key and goes read-only when the environment does. Headless has no settings page, so use one of these there."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "Releases are pushed to npmmirror right after publishing, so the default registry in China serves new versions within a minute as well.\n\nVerify the layer without booting: `dsh --profile web --dump-config` prints a `# == dsh-ai4scholar` section.\n\nThen just ask:\n\n> Find recent papers on CRISPR base editing for sickle cell disease and compare their delivery methods.\n\n> Search PubMed for GLP-1 receptor agonists and cardiovascular outcomes since 2022, sorted by date."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Start",
      "text": "> Which paper is \"Attention Is All You Need\"? Give me its DOI and citation count."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The bundle mounts one row (`id: ai4scholar`) with these defaults. Override from your profile's `cordis.patch.yml` (a patch replaces the whole `config`, so restate every key you keep):\n\n```yaml\n- id: ai4scholar\n  config:\n    apiKeyEnv: AI4SCHOLAR_API_KEY   # credential reference; the key itself never lives in config\n    baseUrl: https://ai4scholar.net"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The API key is resolved **per call** through `ctx.credentials`, so storing or rotating it takes effect on the next tool call without a restart. When the credentials service is absent (a custom composition), the plugin falls back to `process.env[apiKeyEnv]`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The settings card always edits `AI4SCHOLAR_API_KEY` (the browser half does not receive the row config); a deployment that overrides `apiKeyEnv` manages that reference through the environment or the credentials file instead. The session credit tally is process-local (it restarts with dsh); the balance itself always comes from the API."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it fits dsh",
      "text": "- Two halves in one package: the Node half registers the tools; the browser half (`exports[\"./client\"]`, declared by `dsh.client`) contributes the settings card through native `plugins.bundle.config` / `plugins.row.config` slots and `settings.section` (plus `settings.plugin.item` on older hosts) and talks to the Host only through the credentials wire API — the key literal never rides a response, and it never reaches the model.\n- Tools are registered on `ctx.tools` with `defineTool`: typed, schema-validated arguments; a canonical JSON value per call (`{ source, query, total, papers[], truncated, nextOffset? }`); a Markdown rendering for the model; and a `web` result card (structured sources) for the Web UI.\n- A single `tool:ai4scholar` system-prompt section tells the model when to use which platform and to cite by DOI/link.\n- Everything is an effect: unloading the plugin (or editing its config, which triggers HMR) withdraws every tool and the prompt section.\n- No model-visible input is added outside the tool results, so sessions stay fully replayable from the log."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm test          # builds lib/ (Node half via tsc, browser bundle via tsdown), then runs:\n                   #   unit tests, a smoke test against the real ToolRuntime, and a jsdom test that\n                   #   loads the built client bundle under the dsh module-host contract and drives the card\npnpm typecheck"
    },
    {
      "section": "try it in a dsh profile without publishing:",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add /absolute/path/to/dsh-ai4scholar\n```\n\n`dsh plugin add github:<you>/dsh-ai4scholar` also works: the `prepare` script builds `lib/` from source, and pnpm asks you to allow it once via `allowBuilds` in the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- `download_by_doi` / `read_by_doi` resolve through doi.org and known publisher PDF patterns (Elsevier, Springer/Nature, Wiley, T&F, MDPI, IEEE, ACM, ACS, RSC, PLOS, Frontiers, bioRxiv/medRxiv, arXiv). Paywalled articles only download when dsh runs on a network with institutional access; a refusal names the landing page so the user can fetch it by hand.\n- Full-text extraction uses `pdf-parse` (pdf.js) in-process; scanned/image-only PDFs yield an explicit error rather than empty text.\n- The same tool set ships for [OpenClaw](https://github.com/literaf/ai4scholar-plugin-openclaw), [Codex](https://github.com/literaf/ai4scholar-plugin-codex) and [Hermes](https://github.com/literaf/ai4scholar-plugin-hermes)."
    },
    {
